  "question": {
    "text": "A battery of <math><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mtext>&#160;V</mtext></mrow></math> is connected to a resistor dissipating <math><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mtext>&#160;W</mtext></mrow></math> of power. If the terminal voltage of the battery is <math><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mtext>&#160;V</mtext></mrow></math>, the power dissipated within the internal resistance is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.</mn><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>W</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.</mn><mn>072</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>W</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.</mn><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>W</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Emf of the battery,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Potential difference across resister&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Power dissipation in the resister is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p><p>By using Kirchhoff&#39;s voltage law is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is voltage across internal resister.</p><p>Using equation (1) and substitute the given values,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo></math></p><p>Now the ratio of potential across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Now the power dissipation across the internal resistance is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></msub><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p>"
  }
